/**
 * Praxis visualizer augmentations -- no-op runtime.
 *
 * The vendored PyLabRobot visualizer (`../visualizer/index.html`, generated by
 * `web-repl/scripts/vendor_visualizer.py`) unconditionally carries
 *
 *     <script type="module" src="../visualizer-augmentations/index.js"></script>
 *
 * as its last body element. Without this file that tag 404s on every single
 * visualizer page load. The tag is injected by the vendoring script
 * (`_AUGMENTATION_TAG`, vendor_visualizer.py:141), so removing the reference is
 * not an option -- it would be regenerated on the next vendor run. The fix is to
 * make the target exist.
 *
 * DIRECTORY NAME IS LOAD-BEARING: the `<script src>` above is relative, so it
 * resolves only while `visualizer/` and `visualizer-augmentations/` remain
 * siblings under `overlay/assets/` (and, after staging, under `dist/assets/`).
 * See ADR .praxia/docs/decisions/260817_repl-layout-and-delivery-mechanism.md
 * sections 2.1 and 4.2 (row 4).
 *
 * This module is HAND-AUTHORED and never regenerated. Real augmentation content
 * -- state-delta overlays, Praxis-specific chrome, the Python->browser transport
 * hookup -- belongs to Phase 6 slices 2-3, which are out of scope as of 260819.
 * Until then this is deliberately inert: it must not 404, and it must not alter
 * the vendored renderer's behaviour in any way.
 */

// Announce presence so a Phase 6 augmentation can detect a double-load, and so a
// human debugging a blank visualizer can tell "module ran" from "module 404'd".
// `globalThis` (not `window`) because this file is also reachable from contexts
// without a DOM global -- same reason the kernel-side code uses `js.self`.
globalThis.__praxisVisualizerAugmentations = Object.freeze({
  loaded: true,
  noop: true,
  phase: "pre-6", // Phase 6 slices 2-3 replace this module wholesale.
});
